From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MIRAGE <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:25:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] MIRAGE: ps from the deployment's own process list; a tree may
 keep its links' own text

- ps printed one fixed list on every installation (with a mysqld Debian 12
  has not had since MariaDB 10.5), under headers no real ps has. It now reads
  the deployment's list ([mirage] processes, written by the profile generator
  from the hardware class's record of a booted machine and the profile's
  services), adds the session's own sshd, shell and ps, and prints procps-ng
  4's formats for ps, -e, -ef, aux, ax, x and selection by -p, -u and -C.
  Other forms are declined. Without the file the stock command answers.
- grep answers lines typed at a terminal one by one, as GNU grep does.
- createfs records where a symbolic link ends up, as a path from the root, and
  the filesystem reads every relative target from there. A tree that keeps
  each link's own text ([shell] link_targets = verbatim) has its relative
  links read from the directory that holds them.
